#! Inlay hints (s134), under the facsimile profile: `side:` before the `3` of
#! `geometry.area(3)` (a parameter name at a call the checker resolved to
#! a declaration), and `: str` after `who` in `let who = "wolf"` (an
#! inferred binder type). A range that covers no binder and no call
#! answers the empty list. Both classes are on — nothing in this
#! profile's `initializationOptions` turns one off.
name      annotate/inlayHint-facsimile
profile   facsimile

initialize
open      resolve/two_mod/main.lu
wait      diagnostics resolve/two_mod/main.lu
req       inlayHint resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:0-12:0
req       inlayHint resolve/two_mod/main.lu 0:0-9:0
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
req       inlayHint hello.lu 9:0-11:0
shutdown
